# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and rewrites every line ending on
# checkout. Several tests match exact multi-line strings, so a Windows clone of
# this repo failed five suites — gas-proxy, results-paywall, locked-history,
# no-duplicate-functions and email-palette — on a codebase that was fine. The
# files were identical; only the invisible characters differed.
#
# This settles it in the repo rather than in each person's git config, so a clone
# is the same on any machine whatever anyone has set locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.webm binary
